{{also|abdəst}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ep-|id1=water|*ǵʰes-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ota|آبدست}} (modern {{cog|tr|abdest}}), from {{der|en|fa-cls|آبْدَسْت}}, compound of {{m|fa-cls|آب|t=water}} and {{m|fa|دست|tr=dast|t=hand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɑb.dɛst/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-abdest.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑbdɛst|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|ritual}} {{lb|en|Islam}} The [[Islamic]] act of [[wash]]ing parts of the body using [[water]] for ritual [[prayer]]s and for handling and reading the [[Qur'an]].
#: {{synonyms|en|wudu}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|wazukhana}} (place where wudu is performed, South Asia)

====Translations====
{{trans-see|Islamic act of washing parts of the body|wudu}}

